# Cloudflare Pages reads this at deploy time.
#
# The HTML is revalidated every time so a deploy goes live immediately, while
# the images and video — which are only ever replaced under a new filename — are
# cached for a year. That makes a repeat visit cost a few small requests instead
# of re-downloading the hero video.
#
# The stylesheet and script revalidate alongside the HTML. They used to be held
# for an hour, which meant a deploy could leave a visitor running fresh markup
# against stale behaviour: the contact button read "Send on WhatsApp" while the
# cached script still opened a mail client. Since neither file is fingerprinted,
# an hour of that is not worth the two conditional requests it saves — both come
# back 304 and empty when nothing has changed.

/*.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/image/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/video/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/styles.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/main.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
